      "point": "Britannica equates the region with modern Rumelia including Macedonia and Thessaly, while Wikipedia says Rumeli is the Turkish name for Thrace.",
      "quote_britannica": "It corresponds parting with the modern Rumell, which also includes part of Macedonia and Thessaly.",
      "quote_wikipedia": "In Turkish, Thrace is commonly referred to as Rumeli, meaning \"Land of the Romans\", which was the name traditionally given by Turkic societies to the Byzantine Empire and Orthodox Christians."
